{"title":"1970 IMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_November_2024)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remarks (added by pf02, November 2024)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Corrected_Solution_to_Part_(b)_of_the_Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Corrected Solution to Part (b) of the Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/5761114df6fcc5c1e89f4e685bab5a6ad24ecbe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0, a_1, \\ldots, a_n, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"129\" height=\"11\" /> satisfy the condition:\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9ce4180c4ed7487c68fd70c2095c210f1c0b893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 = a_{0} \\leq a_{1} \\leq \\cdots \\leq a_{n} \\leq \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"224\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>The numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/496dba6ce0210ca7bf835089f35151d43ee1b53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{1}, b_{2}, \\ldots, b_n, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> are defined by\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c6bdc15db28ede28ec21e571b260019c6474ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n = \\sum_{k=1}^{n} \\left( 1 - \\frac{a_{k-1}}{a_{k}} \\right) \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a_k}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"208\" height=\"53\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>(a) Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/b/d3b8008c73de3b2a28a681101524efb11debdfd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq b_n &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>(b) given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/e/b9edb2a2ee6fdbfe2c1b954bb4d76626f2dba19f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq c &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />, prove that there exist numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/246f4042a74b62c593886c82f1a7aa204a305141.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0, a_1, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"11\" /> with the above properties such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/1/cf17bbf7a613f863264854bd8e1001c0c987fb12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n &gt; c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> for large enough <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e9b95ce936c65a1ce32c5a018e68dbd5a083b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n = \\sum_{k=1}^{n} \\frac{1 - \\frac{a_{k-1}}{a_{k}} }{\\sqrt{a_k}} = \\sum_{k=1}^{n} \\frac{a_k - a_{k-1}}{a_k\\sqrt{a_k}} = \\sum_{k=1}^{n} (a_k - a_{k-1})\\left(a_k^{-\\dfrac{3}{2}}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -33px\" width=\"471\" height=\"76\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e2f71afa7f9e5e033fd502b7085c7cf10c94927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> be the rectangle with the verticies: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c401077ac34420b6f7a7df8ff3908a41b957259.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{k-1},0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15cc15bd6df8c9abc8eb03737ee1a208e2ffbd4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{k},0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84cb44ff131b4c262219647ba5bbb47830730b6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{k},a_k^{-\\dfrac{3}{2}})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"49\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/d/4ad22d0bf1b454f09c7c0134dda17e137b7c20da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{k-1},a_k^{-\\dfrac{3}{2}})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"48\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/3/01326fe6b79d6f15d0b203fdafa08a7cd4735cc7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph;  size(10cm,10cm,IgnoreAspect);  Label f;  f.p=fontsize(6);  xaxis(0,10);  yaxis(0,1);  real f(real x)  {  return x^(-3/2);  }  draw(graph(f,1,10)); draw((1,0)--(1,1)); draw((1,0)--(2,0)--(2,2^(-3/2))--(1,2^(-3/2))--cycle); draw((2,0)--(3,0)--(3,3^(-3/2))--(2,3^(-3/2))--cycle); draw((3,0)--(4,0)--(4,4^(-3/2))--(3,4^(-3/2))--cycle); draw((6,0)--(7,0)--(7,7^(-3/2))--(6,7^(-3/2))--cycle); draw((7,0)--(8,0)--(8,8^(-3/2))--(7,8^(-3/2))--cycle);  label(&quot;$X_1$&quot;,(1.5,0),0.5*N);  label(&quot;$X_2$&quot;,(2.5,0),0.5*N);  label(&quot;$X_3$&quot;,(3.5,0),0.5*N);  label(&quot;$\\cdots$&quot;,(5,0),N);  label(&quot;$X_{n-1}$&quot;,(6.5,0),0.5*N);  label(&quot;$X_n$&quot;,(7.5,0),0.5*N);  label(&quot;$a_0$&quot;,(1,0),0.5*S);  label(&quot;$a_1$&quot;,(2,0),0.5*S);  label(&quot;$a_2$&quot;,(3,0),0.5*S);  label(&quot;$a_3$&quot;,(4,0),0.5*S);  label(&quot;$a_{n-2}$&quot;,(6,0),0.5*S);  label(&quot;$a_{n-1}$&quot;,(7,0),0.5*S);  label(&quot;$a_n$&quot;,(8,0),0.5*S); [/asy]\" width=\"475\" height=\"475\" />\n</p><p>For all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767a53f43be056f9333f71e3e39f59aa0f8bca35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e2f71afa7f9e5e033fd502b7085c7cf10c94927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/7/ec755878ef6e45e56a6ee82108aff6ba3fb59f55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_k - a_{k-1})\\left(a_k^{-\\dfrac{3}{2}}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -33px\" width=\"152\" height=\"76\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/909a188705bc6b3a8b5143dfd66199933937af87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n = \\sum_{k=1}^{n} [X_k]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"98\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>For all sequences <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e07eb7529a688150b7468c06c49a528f5e0010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ a_k \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> and all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767a53f43be056f9333f71e3e39f59aa0f8bca35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e2f71afa7f9e5e033fd502b7085c7cf10c94927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> lies above the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis, below the curve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/4/404b7820836f0223d3a6f7943beb487ca8f07fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x^{-\\dfrac{3}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"43\" />, and in between the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/d/d8da6e53e9b36b9cac9ba133cef7ecf839b0149f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"10\" />, Also, all such rectangles are disjoint. \n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/9/e39a4fe123eaaaf81e3cb4e4c5a428e315413d02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n = \\sum_{k=1}^{n} [X_k] &lt; \\int_{1}^{a_n} x^{-\\dfrac{3}{2}} \\,dx = \\left[-\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right]_{1}^{a_n} = 2 - \\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{a_n}} &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"448\" height=\"59\" /> as desired. \n</p><p>By choosing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f80ad9a0f4653b8c43fc7352669e9df1f677e5b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k = 1 + k (\\Delta x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/8/5c8dc88654c6c584548c1ee336f349bfeb5d015c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta x &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ffd01cdc48042ce7c67d8edcd4904809831cfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Riemann_sum\" title=\"Riemann sum\">Riemann sum</a> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c168add06c40dc280d6d439b4b28df16efa26002.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int_{1}^{a_n} x^{-\\dfrac{3}{2}} \\,dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"94\" height=\"55\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8ed35007b33e190bea04a656e14464ee81fbf280.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{\\Delta x \\to 0^+} b_n = \\int_{1}^{a_n} x^{-\\dfrac{3}{2}} \\,dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"186\" height=\"55\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/3/633110cc02c13434f353fce7f99abc590e4b7259.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left[ \\lim_{\\Delta x \\to 0^+} b_n \\right] = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\int_{1}^{a_n} x^{-\\dfrac{3}{2}} \\,dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"280\" height=\"56\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37efa14d94532e30191e8dcba65d8bbd66292012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} 2 - \\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{a_n}} = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} 2 - \\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{1+n(\\Delta x)}} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"355\" height=\"45\" />. \n</p><p>So for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/f/7efedbc41c83824431608c97c8cceb2c3f4d5524.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\in [0,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, we can always select a small enough <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/8/5c8dc88654c6c584548c1ee336f349bfeb5d015c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta x &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> to form a sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcf901ecff4e621d50ac1ad4224b20d9d200140e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ a_n \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />satisfying the above properties such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/1/cf17bbf7a613f863264854bd8e1001c0c987fb12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n &gt; c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> for large enough <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> as desired. \n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Remarks_.28added_by_pf02.2C_November_2024.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_November_2024)\">Remarks (added by pf02, November 2024)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Remarks (added by pf02, November 2024)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>1. A remark about the problem: it is not a fair problem.  It is\nnot a good problem for the International Mathematical Olympiad.\n</p><p>The reason is that the problem is trivial for most anyone who\nknows a little bit of integral calculus.  Taken out of its natural\ncontext, it is not trivial.  The young people participating in the\nInternational Mathematical Olympiad are from an age group whose\nmathematical education may not have reached calculus, depending on\nthe country they come from.  Hence, the problem is more a comparison\nbetween mathematical curricula in different countries rather than\nproblem solving ability of young people.\n</p><p>2. The Solution to question (b) of the problem given above is\nincorrect.  Specifically\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/8/0e83d6344157932a13d0ea4b9c6620519cbdbdb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{\\Delta x \\to 0^+} b_n = \\int_{1}^{a_n} x^{-\\frac{3}{2}} dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"182\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>is incorrect.  (To put it bluntly, it makes no sense!)  The upper\nlimit of the integral, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> depends on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/b/1eb29f9de3753a59530941141fcb5c7aa3fa2e38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta x$\" width=\"25\" height=\"13\" />, so it can not\nbe the result of a limit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c2340f8a6691ec36a1bde610dccecf42fe25fb48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{\\Delta x \\to 0^+}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"49\" height=\"28\" />!  In fact, it\nis not even clear what is meant by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eaff592045ef8656a6e8a07e5df28b0e97ed7502.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{\\Delta x \\to 0^+} b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"69\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>The errors and inconsistencies just continue accumulating and\nbuilding up in the remainder of the proof.\n</p><p>3. Below, I will give a corrected proof of part (b) of the problem,\nsimilar to some extent to the idea the author of the Solution above\nmight have had in mind.  Then, I will give a solution which uses\nno calculus.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Corrected_Solution_to_Part_.28b.29_of_the_Problem\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Corrected_Solution_to_Part_(b)_of_the_Problem\">Corrected Solution to Part (b) of the Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Corrected Solution to Part (b) of the Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For simplicity of writing and visualizing, let us denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/2/4529007d3442ff178a17912bf9d65e6b4c8699c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\epsilon = 2 - c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />.\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/d/5dd9e03633a0dc2a60be77adf832c72e22e8670d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 2 - \\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />.  We need to find a sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/c/8acdb05cb79a9c8717989c53e35bca752636986a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_k\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> so that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/9499313db55f6e4eb1da1fbe125ae5b488b86561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n &gt; 2 - \\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> large enough.\n</p><p>We rely on the fact that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff80086121fdcb38835bbeb8f762f862f19a80ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n = \\sum_{k=1}^{n} a_k^{-\\frac{3}{2}} (a_k - a_{k-1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"191\" height=\"53\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Riemann_sum\" title=\"Riemann sum\">Riemann sum</a>\nfor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/7/5d779f952bc9757abf6ce7215f8a6fbb57717456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int_{1}^{A} x^{-\\frac{3}{2}} dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"85\" height=\"46\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a2c753c1899bb6ff2187114bf8d9e54259300a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" />.  The denser the\npoints <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/c/8acdb05cb79a9c8717989c53e35bca752636986a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_k\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />, the better the sum approximates the integral.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/3/6e36152c140839eb6034470a1a3f9479be34f0d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int_{1}^{\\infty} x^{-\\frac{3}{2}} dx = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"121\" height=\"43\" />, we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />\nso that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/a/a4ac3dc741bffb601c5e3190ddd9dd7bdf7027ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 - \\int_{1}^{A} x^{-\\frac{3}{2}} dx &lt; \\frac{\\epsilon}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"153\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we can find a set of points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/2723eae4b263ce248fc57a6f2639b5a9000f6eca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 = a_0 &lt; a_1 &lt; \\cdots &lt; a_n = A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"220\" height=\"17\" />\nin the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/5143570a91863ae3c5898b92fa6cc26411285902.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[1, A]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" />, such that the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Riemann_sum\" title=\"Riemann sum\">Riemann sum</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ffd01cdc48042ce7c67d8edcd4904809831cfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />\ncorresponding to these points is as close to the integral as we want,\nin particular <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0af08db4f0f0909575568b424f2d3b6e6233f930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int_{1}^{A} x^{-\\frac{3}{2}} dx - b_n &lt; \\frac{\\epsilon}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"161\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p><p>This proves part (b) of the problem.\n</p><p>(Note that we don't have to, but we can take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/2661b9993b5163ef33498fa192c1c0489884b5c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k = 1 + k \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" /> as\nsuggested in the Solution.  In fact, we can take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/a/53a0d5298ee2b4c4eb3d648eeb4a8954c4c7b6a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha = (A - 1)/N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" />\nand let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be large enough, to make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> small enough, to make\nthe <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Riemann_sum\" title=\"Riemann sum\">Riemann sum</a> close enough to the integral on the interval\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/5143570a91863ae3c5898b92fa6cc26411285902.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[1, A]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" />.  (Here <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> stands for the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/b/1eb29f9de3753a59530941141fcb5c7aa3fa2e38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta x$\" width=\"25\" height=\"13\" /> in the Solution.))\n</p><p>[Solution by pf02, November 2024]\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This is a solution which does not use calculus.\nTaking in account that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/f/38f017ce4a84ea858bcb5955842d646ebc00b99a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k-1} \\le a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" /> we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/c/60cc8f615f45adf8fa2b16ecc57474fce3ffddf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( 1 - \\frac{a_{k-1}}{a_k} \\right) \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a_k}} =  \\frac{a_k - a_{k-1}}{a_k \\sqrt{a_k}} \\le \\frac{a_k - a_{k-1}}{\\sqrt{a_{k-1}}\\ \\sqrt{a_k}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{a_k} + \\sqrt{a_{k-1}}}{2}} = \\frac{2(\\sqrt{a_k} - \\sqrt{a_{k-1}})}{\\sqrt{a_{k-1}} \\sqrt{a_k}} = 2 \\left( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a_{k-1}}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a_k}} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -24px\" width=\"775\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p>Taking the sum, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/1/af16b6fdfbf0e7235c66e52ad092c3d5e9f33c2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n = \\sum_{k=1}^n \\left( 1 - \\frac{a_{k-1}}{a_k} \\right) \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a_k}} \\le \\sum_{k=1}^n 2 \\left( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a_{k-1}}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a_k}} \\right) = 2 \\left( 1 - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a_n}} \\right) &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"577\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>This proves (a).\n</p><p>To prove (b), let us take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/2661b9993b5163ef33498fa192c1c0489884b5c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k = 1 + k \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/7/777ccac28ecee84f0b6d51a6cd9101ff47650246.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha &gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />. We do similar tricks:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92bb92123011af7f25e3a6a57ad70d37e36207e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( 1 - \\frac{a_{k-1}}{a_k} \\right) \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a_k}} = \\frac{a_k - a_{k-1}}{a_k \\sqrt{a_k}} = \\frac{\\alpha}{(1 + k \\alpha) \\sqrt{1 + k \\alpha}} \\ge$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"424\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/7/8a71402f703e1475cf96ae387a646f7c508d688f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\alpha}{\\sqrt{1 + k \\alpha}\\ \\sqrt{1 + (k+1) \\alpha}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{1 + (k+1) \\alpha} + \\sqrt{1 + k \\alpha}}{2}} = \\frac{2\\alpha (\\sqrt{1 + (k+1) \\alpha} - \\sqrt{1 + k \\alpha})}{\\sqrt{1 + k \\alpha}\\ \\sqrt{1 + (k+1) \\alpha}\\ [(1 + (k+1) \\alpha) - (1 + k \\alpha)]} =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -30px\" width=\"789\" height=\"60\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6f02d9f00f4ce9979d427a0b15d7b88e1bf5c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\left( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 + k \\alpha}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 + (k+1) \\alpha}} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"257\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Now take the sum for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7882a0e547cac0787871bc9e501c7c63bd8faf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1, \\cdots, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e7a1ad8e6c80e212ea7916eeaf26fbf3628deb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n = \\sum_{k=1}^n \\left( 1 - \\frac{a_{k-1}}{a_k} \\right) \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a_k}} \\ge \\sum_{k=1}^n  \\left( \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1 + k \\alpha}} - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1 + (k+1) \\alpha}} \\right) = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1 + \\alpha}} - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1 + \\alpha + n \\alpha}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"719\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p>For simplicity of writing and visualizing, let us denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/2/4529007d3442ff178a17912bf9d65e6b4c8699c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\epsilon = 2 - c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />.\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/d/5dd9e03633a0dc2a60be77adf832c72e22e8670d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 2 - \\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />.  We need to show that we can take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> small enough\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> large enough so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/3/6a3c4e3efa3b823050e2e58d00eaa22cb9abd4aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 - b_n &lt; \\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Start by choosing a value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> small enough to make\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5df57c1fb6fac889109556b7810b3e8075178b8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1 + \\alpha}} &gt; 2 - \\frac{\\epsilon}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"133\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>This can be done since this condition amounts to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e65ac954de71312b1d9c879b199848ae3a1797cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{1 + \\alpha} &lt; \\frac{4}{4 - \\epsilon}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"127\" height=\"40\" />, or in other words to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/9/9393530829da03f14aa9b20866e8372fa6a21f0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha &lt; \\left( \\frac{4}{4 - \\epsilon} \\right)^2 - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"145\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>For the chosen value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> we now choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> large enough so that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/7/037e1ca47cacab06b1bcaa242cac884d7eed1861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1 + \\alpha + n \\alpha}} &lt; \\frac{\\epsilon}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"146\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>This can also be done because the condition amounts to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dcaab758bde65c1c96958557d5e65d0f9eb953d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{1 + \\alpha + n \\alpha} &gt; \\frac{4}{\\epsilon}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"142\" height=\"38\" />, or in other words\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/1/d21804f07fd725b50e0f63995d0a3afab66683fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; \\frac{1}{\\alpha}\\ \\left( \\frac{16}{\\epsilon^2} - 1 - \\alpha \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"175\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>This proves part (b) of the problem.\n</p><p>[Solution by pf02, November 2024]\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO\" title=\"1970 IMO\">1970 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1970 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1970 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1970 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1970 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1970 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1970 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1970 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1970 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017170443\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.043 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.061 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 518/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 20536/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    9.486      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    9.486      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5624:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017170443 and revision id 235665. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}